{
  "thread_id": "thread-001",
  "channel": "teams",
  "messages": [
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:1",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "field_engineer",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:14:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Hi Erkki, I'm at the site now. Changed the SFP on transmission node TRN-042.\nLink is up and alarms cleared, but traffic is still not coming back. Have you seen this before?",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:2",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "expert",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:16:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Yes. Is this one of the older units?",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:3",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "field_engineer",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:16:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Yes, installed around 2019 I think.",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:4",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "expert",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:18:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Ok. Don't trust the green link status on those.\nSometimes after changing the SFP the interface comes up normally, but the forwarding state doesn't recover correctly.",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:5",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "field_engineer",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:18:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "So another SFP?",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:6",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "expert",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:19:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "No. Usually the SFP is fine.\nCheck whether the traffic counters are actually increasing. If they stay at zero even though the interface is UP, it's probably the issue I've seen before.",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:7",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "field_engineer",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:21:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Yes. Link UP. RX power looks normal. Counters basically zero.",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:8",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "expert",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:22:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "That's it.\nDisable the interface, wait a little, then enable it again. Don't reboot the whole unit unless that fails.",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:9",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "field_engineer",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:25:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Did that. Traffic is back 👍",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:10",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "expert",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:25:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Good. These old units sometimes behave like this after an optical module replacement.",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:11",
      "author": "Veikko Vikkelä",
      "role": "field_engineer",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:26:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Is this documented somewhere?",
      "incident": null
    },
    {
      "id": "teams:thread-001:12",
      "author": "Erkki Expert",
      "role": "expert",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-01T09:27:00+02:00",
      "channel": "teams",
      "thread_id": "thread-001",
      "text": "Not that I know of 😄\nWe've just learned it over the years.",
      "incident": null
    }
  ],
